This solution calculates the minimum number of operations required to make all elements in the array `arr` equal. The array `arr` has a length of `n`, and each element is given by the formula `arr[i] = (2 * i) + 1`. The target value to which all elements will be equal is the middle value of the array, which is `n` when `n` is odd, and `n-1` when `n` is even. The function iterates through the first half of the array and calculates the number of operations needed to adjust each element to the target value.

```java
public int minOperations(int n) {
    // Calculate the target value which is the average of the array
    int target = n;

    // Calculate the sum of the first n odd numbers
    int sum = n * n;

    // The minimum number of operations is half the difference between the sum and the product of n and the target
    return sum / 2 - n * target / 2;
}
